WEBVTT

00:47.505 --> 00:51.634
DOONA!

01:01.936 --> 01:03.605
Who is that?

01:16.201 --> 01:17.035
Don't go.

02:00.662 --> 02:01.663
Hop in.

02:45.290 --> 02:48.126
EPISODE 7
CLEAR THE AIR

03:01.598 --> 03:02.557
Why are you here?

03:05.768 --> 03:06.603
Got a cold?

03:16.779 --> 03:18.781
You have a fever. Have you seen a doctor?

03:22.410 --> 03:24.329
What is it you want to say?

03:25.163 --> 03:27.749
Aren't you the one
who has something to say to me?

03:30.793 --> 03:32.086
Let's talk in Seoul.

03:37.425 --> 03:38.760
It's time to make a comeback.

03:38.843 --> 03:40.428
Any longer and you'll be forgotten.

03:41.429 --> 03:42.972
What if I want to be forgotten?

03:45.225 --> 03:48.478
Whether by you or by the public.

03:48.978 --> 03:51.481
What will you do
if I just want to be forgotten?

03:55.568 --> 03:56.694
But you don't want to.

03:57.654 --> 03:59.489
Isn't that what you fear the most?

04:00.073 --> 04:02.283
Being discarded, ending up all alone.

04:05.578 --> 04:06.871
So that's why you did it.

04:08.206 --> 04:12.252
You dumped me in that house by myself
and didn't once show your face…

04:15.255 --> 04:17.215
so I could feel how it is to be abandoned.

04:19.259 --> 04:21.177
It was your way of punishing me.

04:34.357 --> 04:35.400
Stop the car.

04:37.485 --> 04:38.486
I'm getting out.

04:41.322 --> 04:43.950
Stop the car!

04:49.038 --> 04:50.081
Don't.

04:51.666 --> 04:54.168
- Stop it!
- Stop it, Lee Doona!

04:56.546 --> 04:57.672
Stop it!

05:14.564 --> 05:16.774
- What do you think you're doing?
- Let go of me!

05:18.484 --> 05:19.402
Let go!

05:21.654 --> 05:22.655
Let go!

05:26.200 --> 05:27.035
Stop this.

05:28.536 --> 05:29.370
Calm down.

05:33.583 --> 05:34.667
That's enough!

05:43.092 --> 05:44.594
I bet it was fun for you.

05:45.386 --> 05:50.475
Thanks to you, I felt like I was sinking
into the ground every single day.

05:52.560 --> 05:53.644
Don't be dramatic.

05:53.728 --> 05:56.064
You're no better than my mom, you bastard!

05:57.231 --> 05:59.025
You knew I had feelings for you.

06:00.026 --> 06:02.779
You knew how desperately
I was waiting for you.

06:04.113 --> 06:06.908
So you even took advantage
of my feelings to suck me dry.

06:07.784 --> 06:09.911
You fucking disgust me!

06:15.708 --> 06:18.044
You waited for me
because you liked me? Really?

06:20.380 --> 06:21.339
That's not true.

06:21.839 --> 06:23.591
You made a mess you couldn't clean up.

06:23.674 --> 06:25.927
You needed a ticket
to return to the industry,

06:26.010 --> 06:28.554
and I happened to be that ticket.
You never…

06:31.474 --> 06:34.435
Do you even know
what it means to actually love someone?

06:36.646 --> 06:38.773
If you'd really had any thought for me,

06:38.856 --> 06:40.858
you wouldn't have behaved
that way on a stage

06:40.942 --> 06:43.694
that your, my, and your team members'
lives depended on.

06:45.738 --> 06:48.324
Don't act like
you're the only one who got hurt.

06:48.408 --> 06:51.494
I didn't use you.
You were the one who used me.

06:52.870 --> 06:55.206
The person that neglected you wasn't me

06:56.582 --> 06:57.625
but you yourself.

07:03.756 --> 07:04.966
Look at what you just did.

07:08.136 --> 07:10.263
You have no qualms about ruining yourself.

08:02.648 --> 08:03.774
RECENTS

08:03.858 --> 08:05.067
LEE DOONA

08:20.958 --> 08:21.792
Yes.

08:22.502 --> 08:24.337
You're right. It is today.

08:26.088 --> 08:27.632
There's been an incident.

08:28.716 --> 08:30.176
Ms. Lee Doona's guardian?

08:30.676 --> 08:31.594
Yeah.

08:32.220 --> 08:34.597
No, I'm going to make it today
no matter what.

08:35.640 --> 08:36.641
Yes, but

08:37.600 --> 08:39.477
does that really need to be decided now?

08:40.394 --> 08:42.688
Yes. I'll be there soon.

08:44.732 --> 08:47.109
Yes, and look into that hospital
I mentioned earlier.

08:48.653 --> 08:49.487
Okay.

08:55.826 --> 08:59.539
LEE WON-JUN

09:43.249 --> 09:47.962
You have a good relationship
with someone you've known for a long time.

09:48.671 --> 09:50.506
I'm jealous of that.

09:51.340 --> 09:52.758
These aren't mine.

09:57.138 --> 10:01.267
You've gotten better at lying.
Stop contacting me and wait quietly.

10:45.645 --> 10:48.189
RECEIVED TWO TICKETS
FOR TODAY'S LAST BUS TO SEOUL

11:05.331 --> 11:06.499
MOM

11:28.104 --> 11:30.856
Get in the car
unless you plan on never seeing me again.

11:32.608 --> 11:34.485
Those words always scared me.

11:36.070 --> 11:38.489
But somehow,
they’re not at all scary to me now.

11:41.409 --> 11:42.535
Do what you want.

11:43.035 --> 11:45.162
You won’t be seeing me again.

11:51.377 --> 11:53.963
Then why did you come
to the showcase event?

12:55.566 --> 12:59.528
KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE

13:04.158 --> 13:06.243
Jesus, man. Slow down.

13:07.161 --> 13:08.329
What's up with you?

13:11.165 --> 13:13.292
Why is everything so difficult?

13:16.670 --> 13:19.507
Math is the easiest thing
in the world, isn't it?

13:20.549 --> 13:22.301
Maybe for you, asshole.

13:31.018 --> 13:33.270
Who do those kinds of people date?

13:34.438 --> 13:35.272
Who?

13:38.984 --> 13:41.445
I guess they date people like themselves.

13:42.279 --> 13:43.906
Those at the top of their game.

13:46.575 --> 13:47.827
If I were Doona,

13:49.161 --> 13:50.830
I would date Son Heung-min.

13:51.705 --> 13:53.582
Did you see his free kick yesterday?

13:53.666 --> 13:55.918
That kind of trajectory is
impossible to achieve.

13:56.001 --> 13:58.254
That is not the foot of a mere mortal.

13:58.754 --> 14:02.800
I used to be a fan of Messi's.
But now, I'm for Son Heung-min.

15:00.482 --> 15:02.776
RECENTS
LEE WON-JUN

15:23.213 --> 15:25.132
RECENTS
LEE WON-JUN

15:43.567 --> 15:46.904
Then why did you come
to the showcase event?

16:17.559 --> 16:18.519
You dance, don't you?

16:19.019 --> 16:20.354
LEE DOONA

16:25.776 --> 16:26.652
Eighth grade?

16:29.989 --> 16:31.740
All you have to do is to do as I say.

16:32.616 --> 16:35.369
As long as you do that,
you have nothing to worry about.

16:36.078 --> 16:39.248
Once you sign with us,
I'll take care of everything for you,

16:39.331 --> 16:41.959
where you stay,
what you eat, what you wear.

16:43.293 --> 16:46.088
But in return,
you must never hide anything from me.

16:46.171 --> 16:47.506
If you do, we're done.

16:49.091 --> 16:50.342
Why should I do that?

16:52.970 --> 16:54.513
Are we going to be like a family?

16:55.180 --> 16:56.181
Something like that.

16:57.683 --> 16:59.393
Is that easier for you to understand?

17:33.260 --> 17:34.219
Is it here?

17:37.514 --> 17:38.724
Here?

17:51.737 --> 17:52.946
That's enough for today.

18:15.677 --> 18:17.596
This is so good! Wow!

18:25.437 --> 18:26.730
This place is insane!

18:31.443 --> 18:33.946
God, the house feels so empty. Right?

18:40.327 --> 18:41.912
- Yun-taek.
- Yeah?

18:42.412 --> 18:45.124
Well, this person--

18:45.207 --> 18:46.542
Who? A girl?

18:48.210 --> 18:52.256
No, a person was eating beef intestines

18:53.382 --> 18:54.591
and went like this.

18:55.843 --> 18:57.719
Why do you think I keep thinking about it?

18:58.554 --> 18:59.596
What are you saying?

19:05.060 --> 19:06.520
CHOI I-RA

19:28.375 --> 19:29.751
Oh, Jeong-hun!

19:30.502 --> 19:32.754
- Hi.
- That was quick.

19:32.838 --> 19:33.922
You look busy.

19:34.923 --> 19:37.843
- Yeah.
- How did you know I was thirsty?

19:37.926 --> 19:39.136
- Thank you!
- Sure.

19:42.472 --> 19:43.807
That is so refreshing!

19:47.019 --> 19:48.812
What is it you need help with?

19:51.315 --> 19:53.317
It's our department fashion show.

19:53.817 --> 19:56.570
No need to get on stage,
but could you help me with the fitting?

19:56.653 --> 19:59.156
I'll treat you to an amazing meal. Please?

20:02.075 --> 20:03.160
First,

20:03.243 --> 20:06.413
could you try this on for me?

20:06.496 --> 20:07.331
This.

20:07.414 --> 20:10.500
You can get changed over there.
If you can't manage, just holler.

20:12.377 --> 20:13.212
Okay.

20:35.984 --> 20:39.112
Let me ask you this! How could you do
something like that so easily?

20:39.196 --> 20:42.616
That is definitely not true, I-ra.
I've never once given up on you.

20:42.699 --> 20:44.284
My heart has always been yours.

20:44.368 --> 20:45.661
Fuck. What are you on about?

20:45.744 --> 20:48.121
I've finally realized

20:48.205 --> 20:50.832
that you're the only woman in my life.

20:50.916 --> 20:51.750
God.

20:53.126 --> 20:55.128
Have you run out of money?

20:56.463 --> 20:59.466
I'm into someone else now,
you crazy bastard!

21:00.550 --> 21:01.593
Hey, baby.

21:24.658 --> 21:28.036
Can you take a look at this for me?
Is this how it's supposed to be?

21:30.956 --> 21:31.957
- Right.
- I-ra.

21:35.544 --> 21:38.088
Don't do this, I-ra. Let's start over.

21:38.171 --> 21:40.382
What are you doing? You're hurting me!

21:40.465 --> 21:41.550
Please.

21:46.430 --> 21:48.223
Just pay my wife back, asshole.

21:48.307 --> 21:50.684
And hands off
if you know what's good for you.

21:54.646 --> 21:56.898
The sweet smell of money!

21:59.026 --> 21:59.901
Smell it.

22:03.864 --> 22:05.741
Hey! Here!

22:06.616 --> 22:09.494
You've got to do this.
One more time. Oh yeah.

22:11.330 --> 22:12.956
One more time. Oh yeah!

22:52.871 --> 22:53.705
Hi.

23:00.879 --> 23:02.506
Are you back from visiting home?

23:04.299 --> 23:05.258
Yes.

23:05.342 --> 23:06.510
That's good.

23:08.136 --> 23:11.348
When does break start?
You can take about a week off, right?

23:12.224 --> 23:13.600
Shall we go abroad nearby?

23:14.476 --> 23:17.312
Japan? Or Guam?

23:22.609 --> 23:23.735
When did you get back?

23:23.819 --> 23:24.861
This morning.

23:26.738 --> 23:28.657
- And how's your cold?
- I'm okay.

23:31.576 --> 23:32.536
That's good.

23:34.162 --> 23:35.914
I'm going up. I'm tired.

23:35.997 --> 23:38.834
Look, say what you want to say…

23:41.336 --> 23:43.422
and stop being so frustrating.

23:46.883 --> 23:49.386
If I say what I want to right now,
I'll regret it.

23:49.469 --> 23:50.720
So say it.

23:50.804 --> 23:53.014
I can take whatever you say.

23:56.643 --> 24:00.397
Ask me what I did with him.
That's what you want to know, isn't it?

24:00.480 --> 24:01.898
- What?
- Why? Isn't it?

24:01.982 --> 24:04.359
In your head,
you're imagining all sorts of things,

24:04.860 --> 24:07.320
but you don't have the guts
to get mad at me.

24:08.655 --> 24:10.699
Is this your way of saying sorry?

24:12.409 --> 24:13.994
Or are you not even sorry?

24:15.078 --> 24:17.539
What right do I have to get mad at you?

24:17.622 --> 24:20.417
I don't want to know
what you did with that guy.

24:21.042 --> 24:23.128
What I want to know is
what you are doing with me.

24:23.712 --> 24:25.630
I thought it didn't matter to me

24:25.714 --> 24:28.091
whether you're leaning on me
because you're lonely

24:28.175 --> 24:29.342
or just playing around.

24:29.843 --> 24:33.597
Since I liked you and I was okay with it,
I thought it didn't matter.

24:38.018 --> 24:40.020
But I guess I'm not that tolerant.

24:41.688 --> 24:43.607
You don't have to have feelings for me.

24:43.690 --> 24:45.525
Why would someone like you want to have…

24:52.073 --> 24:53.700
But this is going too far.

24:54.784 --> 24:55.785
Even for you.

25:18.225 --> 25:19.059
Hey, Won-jun,

25:19.643 --> 25:22.854
you're staying here over winter break,
right? The landlady was asking.

25:22.938 --> 25:26.191
I'll be moving out. I'll let her know.

25:28.193 --> 25:29.027
What?

25:29.110 --> 25:31.530
Really? Why?

26:24.958 --> 26:26.960
Yes, I'm doing my best to sort things out.

26:27.794 --> 26:30.380
I'll update you as soon as I have news.
I'm sorry.

26:45.061 --> 26:46.146
Why did you do it?

26:48.773 --> 26:49.608
Lee Doona.

26:58.366 --> 26:59.743
I already told you.

27:03.121 --> 27:04.497
I just can't sing.

27:08.793 --> 27:09.628
Fine.

27:11.004 --> 27:12.088
Then take a break.

27:39.240 --> 27:40.075
Yes, Ms. Ma.

27:41.701 --> 27:42.827
It's not going to work.

27:43.328 --> 27:45.664
We'll have to take Doona out
and continue with four.

27:46.164 --> 27:47.040
I'm sorry.

28:20.198 --> 28:21.366
Welcome.

28:55.692 --> 28:56.526
A milkshake?

28:58.403 --> 29:00.780
- You really have given up on everything.
- I have.

29:02.031 --> 29:05.952
I sleep all day,
eat whatever, and do nothing.

29:07.162 --> 29:08.246
So, do you feel smug?

29:09.456 --> 29:10.665
Watching us crash and burn?

29:12.333 --> 29:14.461
I thought I would, but not really.

29:15.503 --> 29:16.755
You should've done a better job.

29:18.214 --> 29:19.466
Tell me about it.

29:20.800 --> 29:23.094
I wish we could have shown you.

29:31.603 --> 29:33.730
About what you said, that you can't sing,

29:35.190 --> 29:36.232
I believe you.

29:39.486 --> 29:40.820
I believed you back then too.

29:44.073 --> 29:47.702
We may not have been friends,

29:48.995 --> 29:51.122
but we were at least comrades in arms.

29:53.124 --> 29:54.334
So I could tell.

29:56.377 --> 29:58.296
I thought you'd be resentful of me.

29:59.422 --> 30:01.257
If you hadn't jumped off then,

30:02.675 --> 30:03.843
I probably would've myself.

30:10.099 --> 30:13.436
I don't hate you. You know that, right?

30:16.022 --> 30:18.566
I wanted to be like you, but I couldn't,

30:20.318 --> 30:22.403
and I didn't want to hate myself for it,

30:23.655 --> 30:25.740
so I think I hated you instead.

30:38.378 --> 30:39.921
10 YEARS LATER GROUND

30:53.393 --> 30:55.144
I'm sorry, we're closed.

31:01.734 --> 31:03.444
I left some of my stuff here.

31:05.905 --> 31:06.739
Come in.

31:25.049 --> 31:27.051
- Sorry, excuse me.
- Oh, sure.

31:49.824 --> 31:51.618
Are you still in your mini-studio?

31:52.702 --> 31:54.954
I found a studio apartment
within only a few days.

31:55.038 --> 31:58.166
It's a bit far from campus,
but it's not too bad.

31:58.666 --> 32:01.419
I feel much better
than when I was commuting from Yangjin.

32:02.337 --> 32:03.671
I'm glad to hear that.

32:05.131 --> 32:06.591
How does it feel to be dating?

32:07.300 --> 32:08.134
Are you happy?

32:14.349 --> 32:16.601
I kept my distance from you for a bit.

32:18.394 --> 32:22.231
You felt like a different person
when you were with her.

32:23.441 --> 32:25.443
Like someone I'd never met before.

32:29.739 --> 32:32.241
I'm saying you've changed in a good way.

32:33.910 --> 32:35.495
I really mean it.

32:36.788 --> 32:40.375
Lee Won-jun who's head over heels.
That's a rare thing!

32:48.257 --> 32:51.970
You are invited to a Churrasco Night
of Unity and Forgiveness!

32:52.053 --> 32:54.472
Place, the house. Time, right now.

32:54.555 --> 32:56.599
- Hostess, I-ra Choi.
- I-ra is so funny.

32:59.602 --> 33:03.064
Do you want to go there?
Everyone will want to see you.

33:06.776 --> 33:07.610
No.

33:10.947 --> 33:12.115
You told me

33:12.615 --> 33:15.034
not to let anyone treat me badly.

33:15.618 --> 33:17.370
But when I thought about it,

33:17.453 --> 33:20.873
I realized I was the one
who mistreated myself most.

33:23.501 --> 33:26.629
I'm treating myself better
by not being friends with you.

33:28.339 --> 33:30.174
It still hurts, you see.

33:34.095 --> 33:35.221
Who knows?

33:35.304 --> 33:39.559
With time, when there comes a point
when all I feel is joy when I see you,

33:40.435 --> 33:42.603
maybe we can be friends then.

33:44.188 --> 33:46.357
Please understand that,
even if you feel disappointed.

34:02.665 --> 34:05.334
In your head,
you're imagining all sorts of things,

34:05.418 --> 34:07.420
but you don't have the guts
to get mad at me.

34:09.338 --> 34:11.340
Is this your way of saying sorry?

34:13.176 --> 34:14.802
Or are you not even sorry?

34:15.595 --> 34:17.472
I thought it didn't matter to me

34:17.555 --> 34:19.891
whether you're leaning on me
because you're lonely

34:19.974 --> 34:21.350
or just playing around.

34:21.851 --> 34:25.521
Since I liked you and I was okay with it,
I thought it didn't matter.

34:28.274 --> 34:30.401
But I guess I'm not that tolerant.

34:49.629 --> 34:50.630
Are you moving out?

34:51.214 --> 34:52.048
Yes.

34:52.548 --> 34:54.634
- Where to?
- I don't know.

34:55.885 --> 34:57.261
What if I told you not to?

35:00.973 --> 35:03.017
- Do I have to answer that?
- Yes, you do.

35:09.190 --> 35:10.525
Could you leave my room?

35:28.584 --> 35:30.962
Stop this. You smell of cigarette smoke.

35:31.045 --> 35:32.380
But I quit.

35:33.339 --> 35:35.091
Maybe it's his smell, then.

35:38.761 --> 35:40.096
You're a real jealous type.

35:41.222 --> 35:44.100
What? Does he not want you?

35:45.143 --> 35:46.519
Is that why you need me again?

35:46.602 --> 35:48.813
I'd stop there,
while I still find it cute.

35:53.818 --> 35:55.194
I'm staying here.

35:56.070 --> 35:58.030
Drag me out if you can.

35:58.114 --> 36:00.491
I'm telling you
I want you out of my sight!

36:00.575 --> 36:02.326
Why are you insisting on being here?

36:02.827 --> 36:03.995
Because I want company.

36:04.078 --> 36:05.788
Which doesn't have to be me!

36:05.872 --> 36:06.706
It does.

36:08.040 --> 36:09.458
It does have to be you.

36:16.132 --> 36:17.758
Then why did you do that to me?

36:19.385 --> 36:20.636
Because I didn't know

36:22.263 --> 36:24.015
that the person I didn't want to lose…

36:26.184 --> 36:27.226
was you.

36:30.354 --> 36:31.647
I don't know a lot,

36:32.273 --> 36:35.276
and I'm always slow
at realizing my own feelings.

36:36.903 --> 36:39.071
I only find out
after I've lost everything.

36:39.655 --> 36:40.948
And then I regret it.

36:42.074 --> 36:43.826
It drives me crazy too.

36:45.745 --> 36:48.289
So, can't you go easy on me, please?

36:50.791 --> 36:53.252
You're a real mess. You know that?

36:54.128 --> 36:55.963
You're selfish and unstable,

36:56.047 --> 36:58.299
and you hurt me without a second thought.

37:00.009 --> 37:01.636
That's why it feels so unfair.

37:02.136 --> 37:04.722
You're the one that came
and shook me up out of nowhere,

37:05.473 --> 37:06.849
but now, I'm the one

37:08.309 --> 37:11.229
who wants you to be mine so much
it's driving me crazy.

37:16.859 --> 37:18.444
So tell me you're sorry.

37:23.282 --> 37:25.368
- I'm sorry.
- Tell me that you like me.

37:27.453 --> 37:29.872
Tell me that you like me and not him.

37:32.875 --> 37:33.751
Please.

37:37.255 --> 37:38.547
I love you.

38:08.786 --> 38:09.745
Won-jun.

38:10.997 --> 38:11.831
Yeah?

38:13.082 --> 38:14.625
Don't hate me.

38:15.835 --> 38:16.961
I don't hate you.

38:18.629 --> 38:21.966
I tried, but I couldn't.

38:23.884 --> 38:25.094
I don't mean now.

38:26.304 --> 38:27.972
I mean going forward.

38:30.016 --> 38:31.142
I promise I won't.

38:34.562 --> 38:36.397
Does this mean we've made up?

38:37.732 --> 38:38.566
Yes.

38:40.026 --> 38:41.485
So easily?

38:42.987 --> 38:46.532
I've always been easy.
I was just pretending to be difficult.

38:56.667 --> 38:59.170
It has to be you for me too.

39:17.271 --> 39:21.275
Do you remember the song
I gave up writing halfway through?

39:22.068 --> 39:24.153
During our second album, I think.

39:26.530 --> 39:28.491
I'd forgotten the melody,

39:29.909 --> 39:31.452
but it's come back to me.

39:34.914 --> 39:36.916
- That's good.
- It is.

39:38.876 --> 39:42.213
To the point where I actually wonder
if it's okay to feel so good.

39:47.343 --> 39:49.095
You should drink that. You ordered it.

42:39.014 --> 42:44.019
Subtitle translation by: Reuben Simpson
